    "content": "## QA Testing Complete\n\nAll 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded. Summary: **15 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\n**Failures found:**\n1. **CS-10** – Job posting form accepts invalid data: a job with minimum salary > maximum salary and zero required skills was published successfully instead of being rejected.\n2. **CS-11** – Duplicate applications with the same email for the same job are accepted instead of being blocked; the duplicate is saved as a second distinct record.\n3. **FT-18** – No edit functionality exists anywhere in the UI for published jobs (only view-applications and delete actions are available).\n4. **IX-19** – App state is entirely in-memory (no localStorage/IndexedDB/backend persistence); any page reload/direct navigation wipes newly posted jobs, submitted applications, and deletions back to the seed data.\n5. **CT-20** – New jobs and applications submitted \"now\" (matching the current date) are labeled \"Yesterday\" instead of \"Today\", indicating an off-by-one relative-date bug.\n\nAll other functional, interaction, and content requirements (browsing, filtering, search, job creation, deletion with confirmation, application submission, dashboard counts/lists, and content completeness) passed verification."
